<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico eases liquidity target - dealers.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico eases liquidity target - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has changed its daily liqudity objective for the money markets, easing the objective to zero from a minus 20 million pesos a day, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The minus 20 million pesos a day objective has been in effect since October 14.</p>
<p>-- Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
